GPU submissions carry their own start/end times (spesgputime, default 1).

all39 (0161): the cache push fell from 33-48 MB / 15-28 ms to 0.3-1.2 MB / ~1 ms a submission,
but the UI is still slow (5-10 submissions a second) and "the GPU worked 0 us" because
redwood_gpu_worked() never measured anything. As msm's a6xx_submit, CP_REG_TO_MEM copies
CP_ALWAYS_ON_COUNTER (0x980, 19.2 MHz) before the indirect buffers and after CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE
into the fence page (GPU 0x011f0800, CPU dma+0xc800), 64 start/end slots by fence. The
RedwoodGPU summary line then says how long the 3D core itself took per submission, which
separates GPU time (clock, 300 MHz) from CPU time in metal2vulkan/Turnip.

